\newlabel{fig:compression}{{6}{19}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {VI-H}}Robustness Boundaries}{19}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{subsec:res_robustness}{{\mbox  {VI-H}}{19}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces External benchmark at three representative SNRs, $480$ shared-realization trials per cell. The $-10$~dB block reports error quantiles because the distributions are bimodal there; the recurring $700$~mm entries are the wrong-basin cluster of that bimodal distribution, i.e.\ a saturated quantile rather than a resolution figure. The PEB row is the root mean square of the per-trial free-Jones PEB, the same statistic plotted in Fig.~\ref {fig:benchmark}; it is a reference for the \emph  {RMSE} (Fig.~\ref {fig:benchmark}(a)) and is not comparable with the median columns, so a median below the RMS PEB reflects a skewed error distribution rather than a bound violation. Catastrophic rates carry exact Clopper--Pearson intervals in the text; runtime and peak RSS are from the serialized single-thread cost suite. The synchronization comparison is reported separately in Fig.~\ref {fig:benchmark_clock}. Best value per column in bold.}}{20}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:benchmark}{{V}{20}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces External benchmark, $480$ shared-realization trials per SNR point. (a)~Position RMSE with the free-Jones PEB. (b)~Median error, which exposes the grid-resolution floor of the sparse baselines. (c)~Catastrophic rate with exact $95\%$ intervals; the proposed route is the only one that reaches $0/480$ and stays there, whereas VBI/SBL and R2 retain a residual outlier mass at every SNR. (d)~Observation-domain reconstruction NMSE.}}{20}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmark}{{7}{20}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces External synchronization comparison on the same paired realizations as Fig.~\ref {fig:benchmark}, $480$ trials per SNR point. The proposed and scale-normalized 4-D clocks are estimated jointly with position; the three external clocks are read from each route's position and per-panel delays through the common map of Section~\ref {subsec:res_benchmark}. (a)~Median (bold) and p95 (faint) absolute clock error: the proposed route tracks the CEB reference, the 4-D route floors in its p95 tail, and the two grid routes floor in the median. (b)~Clock-catastrophic rate ($|\hat  {\Delta t}-\Delta t^\star |>1$~ns) with exact $95\%$ Clopper--Pearson intervals; VBI/SBL carries a persistent $11$--$12\%$ clock outlier mass, the synchronization image of its position outliers.}}{21}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmark_clock}{{8}{21}{}{}{}}
